codex
The rotation failures are reproducible. A 10° turn can clip a cube-sized disc between samples, and a two-obstacle layout makes the default-inflation escape routine choose a turn that clips an obstacle. I also found a heading-cache mismatch. The FSM does attempt to correct lateral goal error in ALIGN, so the 18 mm tolerance needs a handoff test rather than a claim that capture starts immediately.

