codex
The first run confirms failures in rotation checks, reservation coverage, escape safety, lateral “straight” moves, deadline handling, and supervisor revalidation. An ideal rollout of the real segment follower leaves even a 6 mm-inflated reservation after about 0.1 seconds.

I also found a separate FSM issue: at an already-reached goal facing 90°, the planner’s zero-length straight segment is treated as pointing east, so the FSM reports a deviation.

